# Semantics Appendix B: `?ParseNat` reads any natural number written in decimal digits,
# however many: a `Nat` has no bound. Both targets agree past 18 digits and past 64 bits.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
test mod Tests

Parsed: fn Text -> Text
fn Parsed t = match ?ParseNat t:
    ? n: "{n}"
    nil: "nil"
